pra: 0171 GPU draft - the full Mali-T830 change (stages 1-9) as ONE patch

Consolidates gpu-work drafts 0001-0007+0009 (0008 is the tools/mkadt_pra.py
ADT patch and lands as a separate repo commit - NEVER into xnu/patches):
probe (0001), WRITE_VALUE layout experiment (0002), fragment clear (0003),
panfrost quirks (0004), GPU present + SweetFramebuffer hook (0005),
PragueGPU user client + IOAcceleratorES stub (0006), wait-asleep (0007),
recovery (0009). Generated with git diff against the CI-built tree, NOT
chain-collapsed from the drafts.

Why one patch, and why it was regenerated (the 0164 lesson, GPU edition):
the drafts were chain-apply-verified against a scratch tree whose base was
WRONG (a local tree containing patch-stack content CI never had - the same
trap that silently dropped the eMMC patches for weeks; CI applies with
git apply and SKIPS any patch whose context fails, staying green while the
phone runs stale drivers). Against the true CI tree, 0006's
iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp hunk failed context (its anchor was the local
PRAPinctrl entry, which does not exist in CI's table), and 0001 was missing
the extern declaration of prague_gpu_probe in IOKitBSDInit.cpp (a guaranteed
compile failure git apply cannot see). Both fixed minimally in the drafts,
then consolidated from the verified end state.

Reconstruction recipe (0164 method, reproducible):
  1. Pristine xnu-8796.141.3 tarball (apple-oss-distributions tag,
     sha256 f08bfe045a1fb552a6cbf7450feae6a35dd003e9979edf71ea77d1a836c8dc99).
  2. Apply xnu/patches/*.patch with GNU patch -p1 --fuzz=0, every `index `
     line stripped (GNU patch mis-parses them as file creations). The six
     patches CI skips (context failures on the pristine tree) are skipped:
     0031, 0041 (need .sh-staged sources), 0097, 0099, 0127, 0129.
     Cross-check: running the stack with NO pre-skip fails exactly those six.
  3. Apply drafts 0001-0007+0009 onto that tree: zero offsets, zero fuzz,
     zero rejects (see WORKLOG.md for the full transcripts).
  4. This patch = git diff of that end state. Proof (byte-identical, all 7
     files, full-tree diff -rq):
       (CI tree) + this patch == (CI tree) + 0001..0007,0009
     via BOTH arbiters: git apply (CI's actual mechanism) and GNU patch
     --fuzz=0 on the index-stripped file. Local `git apply --check` is NOT
     trusted: git 2.56 skip-detects already-applied patches in some states.
  5. bsd/dev/pra_sdhci.c is untouched (sha256 identical before/after; this
     patch has no section for it; the eMMC 0164 content is not regressed).

Safe-by-construction rule unchanged from the drafts: with no boot-arg
(pragpu=0 default, sweetfb_gpu=0 default) boot behavior is byte-identical
to the pre-GPU kernel - every probe/job/present path is behind pragpu* /
sweetfb_gpu boot-args, the config-table entry is inside
#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_PRA), and prague_gpu.c/PragueGPU.cpp are
wholly inside the same guard. Enable-flag names kept verbatim:
pragpu, pragpu_pa, pragpu_fb, pragpu_wv, sweetfb_gpu,
pragpuaccel, pragpu_selftest, pragpu_sleep_us, pragpu_sleep_present.

Residual risk (see WORKLOG.md): CI's git apply is the final arbiter; the
workflow's Verify step must gain GPU string asserts when this lands, or a
silent skip can never be ruled out from a green run.

